  "aiOverview": {
    "content": "Fortune is a premier global business media brand known for its 500 list, providing in-depth, high-quality analysis of business leaders, technology, and finance. Founded in 1930, it is now owned by Thai businessman Chatchaval Jiaravanon and focuses on in-depth reporting and premium business journalism. Subscriptions, including digital-only and print bundles, are available on their website with various plans. Key Aspects of Fortune Magazine History: Launched in 1930 by Henry Luce during the Great Depression, Fortune was designed to be an upscale business magazine focusing on high-quality writing and, notably, high-quality photography, featuring contributors like Margaret Bourke-White and Walker Evans. Target Audience: The publication targets business leaders, corporate executives, investors, and professionals interested in in-depth market analysis and business trends. Notable Features & Rankings: Fortune 500: An annual list of the largest U.S. corporations ranked by revenue. Global 500: A ranking of the world's largest companies. Most Powerful Women: A highly regarded list and community. Brainstorm Tech: A conference focusing on innovation and technology. Ownership: The magazine is owned by Fortune Media Group Holdings (since 2018), part of the Chatchaval Jiaravanon family office. Subscription Details: While the exact, current, daily-changing rate isn't cited, Fortune provides subscription plans for \"All Access\" which include, but are not limited to, unlimited digital access to the site and the Fortune magazine app, according to the Fortune Newsletters page. Noteworthy Content Fortune provides detailed coverage of topics such as tech regulation (e.g., AI and social media lawsuits), boardroom changes, and macroeconomic analysis. Fortune offers premium newsletters to deliver analysis and insights directly to subscribers.",
